  "rootCause": "stats().calls is the last rendered frame. When a stop is reached, every exhibit that mounts with it reveals in the same frame, and each revealed plinth slot bakes its drei ContactShadows once: a full scene render from a small orthographic camera, in which every hall-sized merged mesh (shell, ceiling slot, wash bays, aisle floor, plinths, cases, beams, brass trim, fixture brass) passes the frustum test, plus the exhibit itself. At verafin (desktop, medium) the steady frame was 49 calls and the reveal frame added the klarup and mysa bakes (9 + 20 and 9 + 12) for 98. At klarup on pixel7 four bakes landed in one frame (116). The drei blur passes draw nothing here (the blur plane sits at the world origin outside the shadow camera), so the bake is one unblurred depth pass; that is unchanged.",
  "fix": [
    "ExhibitFrame: the contact-shadow camera renders only SHADOW_LAYER (7); the slot's crate and exhibit meshes join it when the slot's content becomes final, before the one bake. A bake now costs the exhibit's own calls only (about 9 fewer per slot).",
    "Kit <MergeStatic> (mergeStatic.ts, unit-tested): meshes that share a library material, render order and attribute layout are merged in the wrapper's frame, static instanced meshes expanded per instance; transparent, mirrored, lone and userData.keepUnmerged meshes keep their own calls; sources are hidden, not removed. Triangles unchanged.",
    "Exhibits (R0 grant, merging only): klarup 20 to 8 calls, mysa 12 to 7, wailo 13 to 7, verafin 9 to 5, sdsj 11 to 9. The verafin report grid and the wailo pulse move, so they stay outside the merge. finance-tracker (4), cfia (6), mun (8) and certifications (7) were not touched.",
    "greybox.spec: the draw-call walk records every stop, annotates the table and fails once with all offenders."
  ],
